{"event": "agent", "step": 31, "message": {"type": "bug_report", "screen": "Budget sheet > How it's calculated (opened by tapping Calculated amount card)", "element": "Calculated amount card", "symptom_type": "wrong_value", "field": "Spread over what's left of the period (day count)", "expected": "Budget period 11 Nov to 04 Dec with today 14 Nov has 21 days left (14 Nov to 04 Dec inclusive) and the Days remaining shows 20. Daily split uses 21 days ($40 / 21 = $1.9). Weekly/Biweekly should use the same remaining days, e.g. $40 left over 21 days, so weekly = $13.33 or the spread = $100 / 21 x 7 with consistent days.</expected>\n<parameter name=\"observed\">Weekly split breakdown uses \"24 days\" for \"Spread over what's left of the period\" ($100 / 24 days x 7 = $29.17), i.e. it counts elapsed days from 11 Nov, and \"For next week\" uses \"17 days\". Biweekly calculated amount is $58.33 (= $100 / 24 x 14). Daily split uses 21 days, so the three splits disagree on how many days are left.", "observed_quote": "24 days", "steps": ["Start with budget 100, spent 60 (Groceries 40 + Rent 20), period 11 Nov - 04 Dec, today 14 Nov; Days remaining shows 20.", "Tap the budget pill on the main screen to open the Total budget sheet. Split is Daily: Calculated amount $1.9.", "Tap the Weekly chip. Calculated amount shows $29.17.", "Tap the Calculated amount card to open How it's calculated.", "Read 'Spread over what's left of the period': $100 / 24 days x 7 = $29.17. Read 'For next week': $40 / 17 days x 7 = $16.47.", "Switch to Daily: $40 / 21 days = $1.9. Note the different day counts."]}}
